## What isn't built yet

Every area of the language is built but for what this table lists. A
feature not built yet is `toolchain.not_built_yet` where it is written.
Each area links to its "What is built" topic, which says more.

| Area | Not built yet, or only partly |
|---|---|
| [Project layout and modules](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/project-layout-and-modules-built.md) | Names per domain (partly); Declinable errors (partly); Referenced assets |
| [Values and types](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/values-and-types-built.md) | A map literal with entries; `FileUpload`, `UploadSlot`, `SearchText`, `OAuthGrant`, `AnyObject` and the `Document` base; `jadpo inspect`, showing a built type's final fields and where each came from; `BatchRun`, `BatchProgress`, `RowProblem`, `ImportSummary`, `ExportSummary`, `File` and `FileContents` (partly) |
| [Logic](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/logic-built.md) | All of it |
| [Failures](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/failures-built.md) | Logging |
| [Data](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/data-built.md) | D1, and actions on it as reads first and one checked batch of writes; Other schema changes in `jadpo migrate new`; A worked-out backfill for a field that allows less; A backfill in Jadpo that fills a value held in several columns, or reads a field held so or as JSON; Entities in Redis and record caches (`caches:`); Index kinds other than geographic and HNSW; A database implied only when something needs one; `jadpo rename` |
| [Reads and writes](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/reads-and-writes-built.md) | Reading another store outside an action's transaction; Caches and entities in Redis; Comparing money, ranges and fields kept as JSON in a query |
| [HTTP](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/http-built.md) | Failure wording from a build; `x-jadpo-events`; A route's own `rate_limit:` and the Redis store for rate limits; The `Jadpo-Revision` header |
| [Identity](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/identity-built.md) | `Driver.github`, `Driver.apple` and `oauth_provider:`; A route's `confirm: Confirmation.passkey`; Scope declarations and policy's scope restrictions; OAuth grants: `OAuthGrant` credentials, the connecting and disconnecting routes and `on_behalf_of:` |
| [Policy](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/policy-built.md) | `scopes:`, with the tokens issued to other applications (`oauth_token`, `external_token`); The approval review that shows the report's changes in plain terms |
| [Configuration and time](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/configuration-and-time-built.md) | Unaccepted wording in the approval report; Moving a message to `shared/translations/`; Other members of `clock`, `translations`, `sessions` and `oauth` |
| [External services](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/external-services-built.md) | Walking a list operation's pages with `batches.each`; Services (`runs:`); OAuth grants; The public registry: the protocol, the verifier, publishing, facts, search, advisories and compatibility runs; Importers other than OpenAPI; Choosing a provider when deploying; Erasure at providers |
| [Jobs and events](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/jobs-and-events-built.md) | Publishing chosen public events outward; `batches.each` over a provider's list operation, walked by `page.next`; Each step's state in `jadpo watch`, and in `jadpo trace` with the request timelines, and a record's entry in the personal-data report; Sending the metrics and the alerts' log events to a monitoring tool; The console's timeline; Jitter and `Retry-After` between a delivery's attempts; Splitting a page type allowing more than 1,000 items into batches; `batches.status` and `batches.cancel` with runs in no store or several; a file's run with several databases and none written; `cli.signal_handler_failed` |
| [Testing](https://jadpo.dev/docs/topics/testing-built.md) | Assertion messages (partly); Integration fakes (partly); Watch mode (partly); Data builders, `assert emitted`; Interactive mode; Caches in tests |
